          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Sometimes you can use an ENUM column instead of conventional string types. An ENUM column can store a predefined set of distinct string values. MySQL stores them very compactly, packed into one or two bytes depending on the number of values in the list. It stores each value internally as an integer representing its position in the field definition list, and it keeps the “lookup table” that defines the number-to-string correspondence in the table’s.frm file. Here’s an example:",
